  "description": "LUYYOV crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C108 H108 Dy8 N34 O28. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.722-4.343 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.92-123.23°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C108H108Dy8N34O28. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Dy(III).",
